Mission Local reported that a 16-year-old spent almost three weeks in San Francisco County Jail after allegedly giving law enforcement a false name and birthday. The city took 20 days to verify he was a minor, despite being alerted to the possibility soon after his arrest. During that time, he was kept apart from other inmates in a jail section for people with special needs. A judge later ordered his transfer to juvenile hall on $10,000 bail.

